      "mean_abs_window_offset": 0.042420003563165665,
      "flat_windows_std0": 82,
      "median_power_share_below_1Hz": 0.869
    },
    "cause": "Raw signal is unfiltered with large per-window DC offsets (~0.03-0.04 V) and heavy-tailed amplitude (window std spans ~400x). The global std (~0.053) is dominated by offsets/outlier windows, so after global normalization a typical window has std ~0.0024 around a large constant: the net mainly sees a near-constant offset (subject/session dependent) and the EEG waveform is ~400x below unit scale. Training never left chance: inner-val BCE stayed ~0.693 every epoch and best_epoch was 1 in 3/5 folds (early stopping kept an essentially untrained net); the resulting test AUC<0.5 is noise/offset-driven subject shift, not a label-inversion. No label/prediction misalignment was found (oof[te] indexing and sigmoid direction are correct).",
    "secondary": [
      "no BatchNorm/no per-window scaling, so the tiny-signal regime cannot be fixed by the net",
      "early stopping on val BCE with patience 6 and min_delta, from epoch 1, selects near-initial weights",
      "no augmentation, single 6 s view, pos_weight irrelevant (balanced classes)"
    ],
    "fix_here": "per-window demean + per-window std normalization + clip, BN in models, crop/scale/noise augmentation, early stopping on inner-val AUC, multi-crop TTA within the current window."
  },
